13056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054422 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The sum of three and a number.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054422 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee12fc6a-91b2-5855-96a8-c28bd6652ae5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054422 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the sum of three and a number\" can be written as $3+x$.\n\n**Note:** There are other correct answers as well. We could choose another letter, such as $a$, to represent the number. In that case, \"the sum of three and a number\" could also be written as $3+a$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054423 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13057" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054423 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The difference of eight and a number.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054423 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ebd7ac34-c0e4-5e42-940a-cce33864a7de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054423 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the difference of eight and a number\" can be written as $8-x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054799 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054799 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054799 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ef650886-8d46-583e-bad0-1429ba496479" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054800 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054800 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054800 #edb/ref 1039 "Translating Between Phrases and Algebraic Expressions Containing Addition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054800 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054800 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ae662093-c3e8-5577-af6e-7e2f383da79d" #edb/ref 17592